<title>ITALY: Italy's Genoa sees Dec CPI at 1.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Genoa sees Dec CPI at 1.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>GENOA, Italy 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Genoa said its December consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 1.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In November, Genoa's inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 1.7 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Genoa is one of 10 Italian cities to have published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.88 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0   (0.2)     1.6  (1.7)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0   (0.0)     2.6  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.2   (0.2)     3.0  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.1   (0.9)     4.2  (4.2)</p>
<p>    Furniture			  -0.1   (0.1)     0.3  (0.6)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.0)     1.3  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2   (0.3)     2.5  (2.3)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture    -0.3   (0.4)    -0.4 (-0.9)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (1.4)     3.9  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     1.2  (1.3)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	-0.1  (-0.4)    -1.7 (-1.2)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
